## Inline Syntax

This is _italic_ or {_italic_}.

This is *bold* or {*bold*}.

This is subscript H~2~O.

This is superscript 20^th^.

This is {#highlithed#}. Brace is mandatory.

This is {+insert+}. Brace is mandatory.

This is {-delete-}. Brace is mandatory.

### Smart punctuation

Straing double quotes and single quotes are parsed as curly quotes.

Use curly braces to mark q uote as an opener `{"` or a closer `"}`

To ge a straight quote, use `\'` or `\"`.

`...` -> ellipses

`---` -> em-dash

`--` -> en-dash

### Inline math 

Einstein derived $`e=mc^2`.

### Verbatim

This is `verbatim/code`

### Links

Inline link: [My link text](http://example.com)

Reference link:

[read this too][foo bar]

[foo bar]: https://example.com

Empty label:

[My link text][]

[My link text]: /url

### Auto Links

<https://example.com>

<me@example.com>

### Images

![picture of a cat](cat.jpg)

![picture of a cat][cat]

![cat][]

[cat]: feline.jpg





### Footnote Reference

Here is the reference.[^foo]

### Line break

Line breaks in inline content are treated as “soft” breaks; they may be
rendered as spaces, or (in contexts where newlines are treated
semantically like spaces, such as HTML) as newlines.

To get a hard line break (of the sort represented by HTML’s `<br>`), use
backslash + newline:

This is a soft
break and this is a hard\
break.

